{"t":51,"type":"node.request","node":".","to":"assets","what":"In this world, whenever you brake for someone, your kart gets *faster*.\nA volt brakes for a stalled kart and surges. A thrower stops before hitting two riders and practically *flies*.\nBecause of this, racers fight over who gets to be *polite*.\nBut thirteen-year-old *Ben* brakes beside every rival, and his kart never speeds up.\nThen one race, he brakes before the drop and shoots past the *leader*.\nHe brakes beside her again. Nothing. Again. Nothing. His lap takes exactly *ninety* seconds.\nBen circles back and watches her kart skid toward the *drop*.\nBen *froze*. She had been sliding before, too.\nThe track never rewarded brake pedals. It rewarded *kindness*.","requestId":"q1"}
